      "body": "Adrian\u2018s review from IVY ML\n\n===\n\nSection 1.2 bulleting is slightly broken. I think OLD\n   * data node The following\nNEW\n   * data node\n\n The following\nEND\n\n---\n\n1.2\ns/[RFC8340]../ [RFC8340]./\n\n---\n\nUse of BCP14 boilerplate. There doesn't seem to be any use of BCP14 language in the document, so you can/should remove the boilerplate in section 2 and in the main description clause in the YANG model.\n\n---\n\n3.\ns/e.g. /e.g., /  (twice)\n\n---\n\nFigure 1\ns/e.g.,SW/e.g., SW/\n\n---\n\n6.\nYou have a non-ASCII 'smart' character.  \"needed\u00e2\u20ac\u201dsuch\"\n\n---\n\n7. identity ne-software\nProbably expand \"a.k.a.\"\n\n---\n\n7. identity software-module\ns/e.g. /e.g., /\n\n---\n\nI would appreciate some explanation of the two software statuses. \"Installed\" is pretty obvious, but \"Activated\" could use a few words.\n\n---\n\nThe document doesn't include an Operational Considerations section (per draft-ietf-opsawg-rfc5706bis). Inclusion of such a section is not mandatory, but it could be helpful even in a YANG model document that is clearly all about network operations.\n",
